The adapted Mamba2Reference uses pure PyTorch causal convolution, gated RMS
normalization, and a scalar state recurrence. It retains the upstream default
SLiM Mamba2 parameter layout, with no fused/distributed/generation-cache code.
A sequence-length guard limits CPU reference work. The native backend imports
the original mamba-ssm==2.2.2 package explicitly and performs no fallback.
This adaptation has not been validated for native CUDA numerical parity.

WAFT feature extraction and full five-update consumer follow the official WAFT architecture.
